<!-- shortcode start note -->
<div class="bg-skye-light p-4 mb-4 [&>p:last-child]:mb-0 [&>h3]:mt-0 rounded-lg" role="alert" ><h3 class="font-bold text-base">Note</h3><p><p>As an alternative, you can also use the following command with the Upsun Fixed CLI to find out where a given region is hosted:</p>
<div class="relative" data-engagement-id="content-codeblock">
<div class="highlight"><pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"><code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"><span class="line"><span class="cl">platform api:curl regions <span class="p">|</span> jq <span class="s1">&#39;.regions[] | select(.available)  | .id + &#34;: &#34; + .provider.name + &#34; - &#34; + .zone + &#34; - &#34; + .timezone&#39;</span> <span class="p">|</span> sort</span></span></code></pre></div>
</div>
<p>The returned list contains, for each available region, its name, provider, geographic zone and its timezone - as shown above.</p>
</p>
